"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1387977-i20220328","date":"2022-03-28","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905853818","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905853818","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-03-28","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1387977-i20220309","date":"2022-03-09","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":3,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905853817","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905853817","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-03-09","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1387977-i20220309-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1601","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1387977-i20220309","date":"2022-03-09","original_code":"746.1601","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-03-28","finding":"Child/ Caregiver Ratio - 13 or More Children: I observed 11 children who were 18 months-2 years old being supervised by only one caregiver.   There must be no more than 9 children per 1 caregiver for children 18-23 months old.  One child had been sent over there from the 2 year old class by his caregiver because the child wanted to go.  I informed her that he must come back to his own classroom as that caregiver already had too many children in her class without that extra one.    CHILD CAREGIVER RATIO MUST BE IN COMPLIANCE BY THE COMPLIANCE DATE INDICATED.  A FULL PERMIT WILL NOT BE ISSUED WTIHOUT PROPER CHILD CAREGIVER RATIO IN PLACE.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026466682","violation_type_title":"Child/ Caregiver Ratio - 13 or More Children (26 TAC §746.1601)","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1387977-i20220309-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3701","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1387977-i20220309","date":"2022-03-09","original_code":"746.3701","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-03-28","finding":"Safety - Areas Free From Hazards: The utility room outside the building has cleaners  detergents, plastic liners in there.  The room will not lock to keep these hazards inaccessible to the children.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026225879","violation_type_title":"Safety - Areas Free From Hazards (26 TAC §746.3701)","topic_label":"Safety hazards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1387977-i20220309-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3301-f","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1387977-i20220309","date":"2022-03-09","original_code":"746.3301(f)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-03-28","finding":"Nutrition and Food Service - Drinking Water Available and Served: I observed the 4 year olds having snack when I arrived.  They were having graham crackers and milk.  You must ensure a supply of drinking water is always available to each child at every snack, mealtime, and after active play and is served in a safe and sanitary manner.  I explained this and the children were given water at that time.  I spoke to the person who makes the snacks to send to the classroom and she said she will start sending a pitcher of water as well as milk to the classrooms for snack.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026225880","violation_type_title":"Nutrition and Food Service - Drinking Water Available and Served (26 TAC §746.3301(f))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1387977-i20220105","date":"2022-01-05","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,